00Z","completedAt":"2026-11-26T11:01:49.200Z","tokenUsage":{"usedTokens":40200,"maxTokens":1000000,"inputTokens":39300,"outputTokens":900,"updatedAt":"2026-11-26T11:01:49.200Z"},"model":"claude-opus-5-5"}],"runtimeRequests":[],"messages":[{"createdBy":"user","creationSource":"mobile","id":"message:rich:user:1","threadId":"thread-rich","runId":"run:rich:1","nodeId":"node:rich:1:root","role":"user","text":"Where does Tidewise compute the predicted tide height? I want to understand the harmonic model before I touch it.","attachments":[],"streaming":false,"createdAt":"2026-11-26T11:00:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-26T11:00:00.000Z"},{"createdBy":"agent","creationSource":"mobile","id":"message:rich:assistant:1:1000006","threadId":"thread-rich","runId":"run:rich:1","nodeId":"node:rich:1:root","role":"assistant","text":"The prediction lives in `HarmonicPredictor.height(at:)` in `Sources/TideKit/HarmonicPredictor.swift`. It sums the station's tidal constituents:\n\n```swift\nfunc height(at date: Date) -> Double {\n  let hours = date.timeIntervalSince(epoch) / 3600\n  return datumOffset + constituents.reduce(0) { sum, c in\n    sum + c.amplitude * cos((c.speed * hours + c.phase) * .pi / 180)\n  }\n}\n```\n\nEach constituent (M2, S2, K1, O1, …) comes from the station's entry in `config/stations.json`. `TideTable` calls this every six minutes to build a day of heights, and `TideChartView` draws that table.","attachments":[],"streaming":false,"createdAt":"2026-11-26T11:00:08.400Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-26T11:00:08.400Z"},{"createdBy":"user","creationSource":"mobile","id":"message:rich:user:2","threadId":"thread-rich","runId":"run:rich:2","nodeId":"node:rich:2:root","role":"user","text":"Run the predictor tests so we know where we're starting from.","attachments":[],"streaming":false,"createdAt":"2026-11-26T11:00:48.400Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-26T11:00:48.400Z"},{"createdBy":"agent","creationSource":"mobile","id":"message:rich:assistant:2:2000004","threadId":"thread-rich","runId":"run:rich:2","nodeId":"node:rich:2:root","role":"assistant","text":"All 4 TideKit tests pass:\n\n```bash\nswift test --filter TideKitTests\n```\n\nThat covers high water at Port Hollis, the datum offset, the six-minute table spacing and extrema ordering. Nothing tests the low-water times yet, which is where the drift you mentioned would show up.","attachments":[],"streaming":false,"createdAt":"2026-11-26T11:00:58.500Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-26T11:00:58.500Z"},{"createdBy":"user","creationSource":"mobile","id":"message:rich:user:3","threadId":"thread-rich","runId":"run:rich:3","nodeId":"node:rich:3:root","role":"user","text":"Write up a plan for caching station data offline. Use whatever formatting makes it easy to scan.","attachments":[],"streaming":false,"createdAt":"2026-11-26T11:01:38.500Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-26T11:01:38.500Z"},{"createdBy":"agent","creationSource":"mobile","id":"message:rich:assistant:3:3000004","threadId":"thread-rich","runId":"run:rich:3","nodeId":"node:rich:3:root","role":"assistant","text":"Here's a plan for keeping station data available offline.\n\n## Cache layout\n\n1. **Stations**: one JSON file per region under `Caches/stations/`.\n   - Written after every successful refresh.\n   - Read at launch before the network answers.\n   - [x] Already decodable with `Station.Codable`\n   - [ ] Needs a version field\n2. *Predictions* are cheap to recompute, so `TideTable` is never cached; ~~store a week of tables~~ was the first idea.\n3. Constituent updates come from https://tides.example.test/harmonics and the [station feed](https://tides.example.test/feed).\n\n> The cache is a convenience, not a source of truth: if it fails to decode, delete it and refetch.\n\n| File | Size | Refresh |\n| :--- | :---: | ---: |\n| `north.json` | 18 KB | weekly |\n| `inlet.json` | 9 KB | weekly |\n| `south.json` | 21 KB | monthly |\n\n```swift\nstruct StationCache: Sendable {\n  let directory: URL\n  var version = 2 // bump when Station's shape changes\n  func load(region: Region) throws -> [Station] { … }\n}\n```\n\n```bash\n# Inspect what a device has cached\nxcrun simctl get_app_container booted com.example.tidewise data && ls Library/Caches/stations\n```\n\n```json\n{\"version\": 2, \"region\": \"inlet\", \"stations\": [\"port-hollis\", \"kettle-point\"]}\n```\n\n---\n\nThat's everything. Say the word and I'll start with the version field.","attachments":[],"streaming":false,"createdAt":"2026-11-26T11:01:49.200Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-26T11:01:49.200Z"}],"plans":[],"turnItems":[{"id":"turn-item:message:message:rich:user:1","threadId":"thread-rich","runId":"run:rich:1","nodeId":"node:rich:1:root","providerThreadId":"provider-thread:rich","providerTurnId":"provider-turn:rich:1","nativeItemRef":null,"parentItemId":null,"ordinal":1000001,"status":"completed","title":null,"startedAt":"2026-11-26T11:00:00.000Z","completedAt":"2026-11-26T11:00:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-26T11:00:00.000Z","type":"user_message","createdBy":"user","creationSource":"mobile","messageId":"message:rich:user:1","inputIntent":"turn_start","text":"Where does Tidewise compute the predicted tide height? I want to understand the harmonic model before I touch it.","attachments":[]},{"id":"turn-item:rich:1000002","threadId":"thread-rich","runId":"run:rich:1","nodeId":"node:rich:1:root","providerThreadId":"provider-thread:rich","providerTurnId":"provider-turn:rich:1","nativeItemRef":null,"parentItemId":null,"ordinal":1000002,"status":"completed","title":"Workspace ready","startedAt":"2026-11-26T11:00:00.400Z","completedAt":"2026-11-26T11:00:00.600Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-26T11:00:00.600Z","type":"command_execution","input":"Preparing workspace","outputOmitted":true,"exitCode":0},{"id":"turn-item:rich:1000003","threadId":"thread-rich","runId":"run:rich:1","nodeId":"node:rich:1:root","providerThreadId":"provider-thread:rich","providerTurnId":"provider-turn:rich:1","nativeItemRef":null,"parentItemId":null,"ordinal":1000003,"status":"completed","title":"Thinkin